as true at 1.56 (5-1¼) metres, with all three still jumping at 1.58 (5-2¼), but Catherwood won the gold medal when only she could clear that height. She then succeeded on her third attempt at 1.60 (5-3) to break the world record. However, the bar was re-measured for record purposes, and the final mark was given as 1.595 metres (5-2¾)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "There was a jump-off for silver/bronze between Gisolf and Wiley, with Gisolf winning silver, although details are not known. There was also a jump-off for 4th through 10th place among seven jumpers, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/77967"} "Jean Shiley"] " clearing 1.51 metres to take fourth, although further details are unavailable."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "676"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/65828"} "Ethel Catherwood"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "1.40 (=1)"] [:td {} "1.595 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "345"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/73730"} "Lien Gisolf"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "1.40 (=1)"] [:td {} "1.56 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "587"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78011"} "Mildred Wiley"]] [:td {} [:a